5. How handle db error in nodejs If db not return any response

If the database doesn't respond, I would handle it using a connection timeout and query timeout rather than allowing 
the request to wait indefinitely.

I would catch the database error in the service or repository layer and pass it to centralized error-handling middleware. 
I would also configure connection pooling and monitor database health.

For temporary failures, I can use limited retries with exponential backoff, but I wouldn't retry every error because 
it can increase database load.

Finally, I would return an appropriate 503 Service Unavailable response to the client and log the failure for monitoring.
