6. SQL vs mongoDb

I choose SQL when the application has structured and relational data where relationships, transactions, and strong consistency 
are important. 

For example, in an appointment booking system, users, doctors, appointments, and payments have clear relationships, 
so I would prefer PostgreSQL or MySQL.

On the other hand, I choose NoSQL when the data structure is flexible, frequently changing, or doesn't require 
complex relationships.

For example, in an e-commerce application, product details may vary across categories. A mobile phone has RAM and storage, 
whereas a shirt has size and color. I would prefer MongoDB because it supports flexible document structures.

So, my choice depends on the data structure, relationships, transaction requirements, scalability, and query patterns, 
rather than simply choosing one database over the other.



